---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { calls } from '../lib/site';
import { href } from '../lib/paths';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="What Good Call is, who it is for, how answers are judged and what it cannot do."
  path="/about/"
  back={{ href: href('/'), label: 'Back' }}
>
  <h1>About Good Call</h1>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Good Call is practice for judgement. Each scenario is a moment where the right thing to do is not obvious, or is
      obvious and still hard. You choose, and then you see the reasoning.
    </p>
    <p>
      It starts with consent, because that is where a bad call does the most harm, and because it is for everyone.
      Anyone can misjudge a situation. Anyone can have their own boundary ignored.
    </p>
    <p>
      The work scenarios are for people preparing for job applications and training, especially anyone who does not get
      the extra time or support to prepare. That includes many neurodivergent applicants. Timed tests reward people who
      already know the unwritten rules. Good Call writes the rules down.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="judged-title">
    <h2 id="judged-title">How answers are judged</h2>
    <p>Real situations are rarely just right or wrong, so there are three verdicts:</p>
    <ul class="ticks">
      <li><span><b>{calls.best.label}.</b> The choice that respects everyone involved and solves the problem.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>{calls.okay.label}.</b> It avoids the worst outcome but leaves something undone.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>{calls.risky.label}.</b> It is likely to hurt someone, or you.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p>Every answer has its reason. The reason is the point, not the score.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
    <h2 id="limits-title">What this is not</h2>
    <ul class="ticks">
      <li>Not legal advice. Where a law is mentioned, it is the law in England and Wales unless it says otherwise.</li>
      <li>Not a qualification. Finishing a set does not certify anything.</li>
      <li>Not a mark scheme. Employers score their own tests in their own way.</li>
      <li>
        Not yet reviewed. These scenarios are first versions. They have not been checked by a consent educator, a
        lawyer or a recruiter.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <h2 id="privacy-title">Your answers</h2>
    <p>
      Your answers and reading settings are saved in this browser only. Nothing is sent anywhere, there is no account
      and no tracking. Use "Clear my answers" on a set's page to remove them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p class="credit">by <a href="https://rolandcorreia.com">Roland Correia</a></p>
</Base>
